// npm dependency audit: `npm run audit:npm`. See "Dependency audit" in
// DEVELOPMENT.md for the policy and for how to add an exception.
//
// Fails on high and critical advisories, in dependencies and
// devDependencies alike. Every allowlist entry needs a comment block above it
// with the advisory, why it can't be fixed yet, how it does or doesn't reach
// HoploDex, and a date to look at it again. Scope entries to the analysed
// dependency path (`GHSA-…|path`) rather than the bare advisory ID, so the
// same advisory arriving by another route fails the audit again.
{
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "high": true,
  "report-type": "summary",
  "allowlist": [
    // extract-zip: symlink path traversal and arbitrary file writes when
    // unpacking a crafted zip (GHSA-7pqw-9j4j-h8q3, GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv).
    //
    // No fix in WebdriverIO 9: every extract-zip release is affected, and
    // @wdio/utils 9.32.0 (the last 9.x) requires @puppeteer/browsers ^2.
    // WebdriverIO 10 (2026-10-07) moved to @puppeteer/browsers 3, which no
    // longer uses extract-zip, but it is a breaking major not yet taken.
    //
    // Not reachable. Dev-only (E2E tooling); nothing ships in the app.
    // @puppeteer/browsers only unzips a Chrome or Firefox download, which
    // WebdriverIO fetches when it has to start a browser itself. @wdio/cli
    // loads the module that imports it, but neither of its callers gets that
    // far: the launcher's setupBrowser() and each worker's startWebDriver()
    // see a remote driver, because e2e/wdio.conf.ts sets the hostname (and
    // each worker's port) of the app's own embedded WebDriver server, and the
    // browserName is "wry", not chrome or firefox.
    //
    // Review by 2026-12-31, or with the move to WebdriverIO 10 (#86), which
    // removes this path.
    "GHSA-7pqw-9j4j-h8q3|*@wdio/utils>@puppeteer/browsers>extract-zip*",
    "GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv|*@wdio/utils>@puppeteer/browsers>extract-zip*",

    // braces: stack exhaustion (denial of service) when expanding deeply
    // nested brace patterns (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm, <= 3.0.3).
    //
    // No fix: 3.0.3 is braces' latest release and is affected. WebdriverIO
    // 10's @wdio/mocha-framework takes mocha 12, whose chokidar 5 no longer
    // uses braces, but it is a breaking major not yet taken.
    //
    // Not reachable. Dev-only (E2E tooling); nothing ships in the app. Mocha
    // uses chokidar only for its command line's watch mode
    // (lib/cli/watch-run.js), and WebdriverIO runs mocha through its API, so
    // that code is never loaded, let alone given input from a document, a
    // database or the network.
    //
    // Review by 2026-12-31, or with the move to WebdriverIO 10 (#86), which
    // removes this path.
    "GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm|*@wdio/mocha-framework>mocha>chokidar>braces*",
  ],
}
